# Literals of the IVSN v1 snapshot container and its schema (plan 08-09, D-13, D-38). Hand-derived on paper before any serializer exists:
# these are repeatability pins of a project-written text, never evidence that the text is correct. The container is specified in
# docs/formats/ivsn-v1.md; each line is `<key> <value>`.
# schema-digest-sha256 is the SHA-256 of the exact bytes of data/state/schema.literal.txt (the canonical descriptor text of the 88 rows of
# the digest field table, the preimage of the schema digest in the container header). The gate step state recomputes it with cmake -E
# sha256sum (token state-schema-stale), so a change of the literal without a deliberate re-pin fails the gate; plan 08-11 requires the
# writer to produce the same digest from the table.
schema-digest-sha256 6cd4932f5ebf0b0fc2377555ca079d0313bb27a4df1a4fda9e15f37c6eb1d193
#
# Plan 08-09 task 2: the sizes of the container, derived on paper from the table text (docs/formats/ivsn-v1.md, "Size derivation"). A section is
# 7 bytes of frame (the text IVSD, the domain, the domain version) plus its STATE rows; an array row costs 4 bytes of count plus count x width.
# header-bytes: 24 fixed bytes + 32 schema digest + 64 profile id + 32 parameter digest + 3 x 40 slot records + 32 composite digest + 7 x 44 section entries.
header-bytes 612
# trailer-bytes: one SHA-256 over every earlier byte.
trailer-bytes 32
# section-bytes.<name>: CPU 7 + (4 + 8 x 2) + 8 x 1 = 35; MEM 7 + 8 + 1028 + 516 + 1028 + 36 + 6 + 132 = 2761; INSTANCE 7 + 12 + 68 + 528 = 615;
# VIDEO 7 + 36 + 8 = 51; AUDIO 7 + 36 + 8 + 8 + 4 = 63; INPUT 7 + 20 + 8 + 8 + 36 = 79; PSGLOG 7 + 36 + 8 = 51.
section-bytes.cpu 35
section-bytes.mem 2761
section-bytes.instance 615
section-bytes.video 51
section-bytes.audio 63
section-bytes.input 79
section-bytes.psglog 51
# sections-total-bytes: 35 + 2761 + 615 + 51 + 63 + 79 + 51.
sections-total-bytes 3655
# total-bytes: 612 + 3655 + 32.
total-bytes 4299
# section-offset.<name>: 612 plus the lengths of the sections before it, in the order cpu, mem, instance, video, audio, input, psglog; the trailer starts at 4267.
section-offset.cpu 612
section-offset.mem 647
section-offset.instance 3408
section-offset.video 4023
section-offset.audio 4074
section-offset.input 4137
section-offset.psglog 4216
trailer-offset 4267
# header-prefix-hex: the first 24 header bytes, written by hand: the magic 89 49 56 53 4E 0D 0A 1A, format version 0001, flags 0000, total_bytes 000010CB (4299),
# schema version 00000001 and section count 00000007.
header-prefix-hex 894956534E0D0A1A00010000000010CB0000000100000007
#
# Plan 08-11 Task 1 (appended; every line above is frozen oracle data of plan 08-09 and is not edited): the profile parameter digest of the registered
# profile, the SHA-256 over the four ASCII bytes IVSP, a big-endian u16 1 and the four table body digests in the order memory map, PSG, STIC, controller
# (docs/formats/ivsn-v1.md, "Profile identity"). Each body digest is the SHA-256 of the text that the generator of that table writes for the profile, with
# its comments removed: a cite, tag or provenance string of a profile file is in none of them. Repeatability only: this is a repeatability pin of the
# current profile files, never evidence that the tables are right (a changed table value changes it on purpose, a changed cite string changes nothing).
# The value was first computed by a scratch script outside the tree from the generated includes; the test state.literal.params-digest holds the core to
# it and to a second rebuild of the preimage.
params-digest-sha256 89ad65073a3e357acbdd687f6a29016457864a1666b953e9327b7559dc0c0522
